The issue is that `lastTick = performance.now()` in `startGameLoop()` sets it to the current time, but the rAF callback fires almost immediately with a timestamp that's close. Let me look at the game loop:

```js
function gameLoop(timestamp) {
  if (!gameRunning) return;
  animFrameId = requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop);
  if (timestamp - lastTick >= TICK_MS) {
    lastTick = timestamp;
    tick();
    render();
  }
}
```

